; 2 - Branch distance backward
; Backward, a branch reaches exactly 128 bytes (from the next
; instruction). For BSR the message suggests JSR, otherwise JMP.
;
; Try it:
;   - Hover over Back (line 12): address $00.
;   - Change "RMB 125" in line 13 to "RMB 123": then BEQ (line 15)
;     is exactly -128 and OK, only BSR (line 16) is still too far.
;   - JMP and JSR (lines 17, 18) jump to an absolute address: always OK.

            ORG     $00
Back        NOP                     ; OK: address $00
            RMB     125             ; OK: space $01..$7D
            BRA     Back            ; OK: at $7E, next $80, -128
            BEQ     Back            ; ERROR: at $80, next $82, -130
            BSR     Back            ; ERROR: -132 - suggests JSR
            JMP     Back            ; OK: absolute jump
            JSR     Back            ; OK: absolute subroutine call
